title the red everyone believed was booked -- the width gate greens, and the ceilings fall to hold it
prompt kg; reds-first pointed at the width gate red all night, which every reading had called another body's booked lap; measurement found no row anywhere.
think The belief was the defect: 331 files and 1,265 flagged lines stood over ceilings of 329 and 1,263 with no ledger row owning the drift, so the fleet's one full-tree width gate refused at every roster pass while every seat deferred to a booking that did not exist. The repair rode the ratchet's own on-touch law: the flagged roster's one-hit files included brushstroke/tokens.rye and brix/infuse.rye -- both on tonight's own touch path, the face dressing through one and the theme cascade through the other -- each carrying var sp: usize as a line-scan index under a seam comment the scan's markers never granted. Both migrated to u32 with the width law's said-why (the index coerces at the slice edge), the corpus fell to 328 and 1,262, the ceilings fell with it, and width-check answers verdict=ok at the new floor -- proven alongside the face witness GREEN over both touched modules and TAME clean. Booked and closed as REDS %350, fetch-first, with the lesson named: a red every seat believes is booked is a red nobody owns.
obs The gate had been red since before the mul lap; every one of tonight's full-roster readings carried it. The fleet's roster count should read one more green at the next round-open.
